## Not in this phase

- **Linux parity** for any of the above (D63).
- **UI built in HTML.** D2 still excludes it; D64 allows only hosting the OS's b rowser view as content.
- **UI Automation** (Windows accessibility for our drawn UI). The hosted RichEdi t and WebView2 bring their own providers; the drawn UI stays unannounced to Narr ator. It is a phase of its own (the N7 bridge, ported); see Risks.
- **A local [7mterm[27minal** (ConPTY, `forkpty`). a3-app's [7mterm[27minal is remote: bytes c ome over the agent's WebSocket. `[7mterm[27m` is the emulator only.
- **DirectComposition.** Panels on Windows are opaque with DWM corners and shado w; hosts are child windows (D66). Transparent panels and visual-hosted WebView2  :[K[K[?1l>[?1049l